Z||000000||ChadMan||10-30-2000||08:42 AM||||I ordered and installed the Fiero Store's catalytic converter kit for my 88 Coupe - it came with a "high-flow" (their claim - probably true) Walker cat and a patch pipe.  The patch pipe got "fat" on the end, so I cut that part off and used it as a collar to join the cat to the existing exhaust.<P>I have a nice tight seal where the head pipe joins the patch pipe, where the patch pipe joins the cat, and where the cat joins the collar.  But the collar is too big where it joins the rest of the exhaust - looks like the collar is about 2.25" I.D. and the pipe is 2" O.D.  It's too big a gap to crimp down with a clamp.<P>Any ideas or suggestions before I give up and take it to Tuffy?||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||10-30-2000||09:44 AM||||You should be able to get a sleeve at the auto parts or at Tuffy for next to nothin'.||||reg||3
